{"author":"schacon+claude-opus@gmail.com","body":"af9e2e4b2 (+ 4960f712, 6d6d798, a1724e3, b43fa4a); 39/56 passing (was 19). Fixed: (1) submodule add of existing repo no longer detaches source HEAD (was the big one - stale branch ref made downstream submodule fetch find no new commits); (2) clone stores verbatim URL (cwd-joined, no canonicalize) so 'From <url>' matches git (super shows /., submodule shows no /.); (3) submodule.recurse config triggers recursion; (4) recurse into unpopulated changed submodules (--work-tree=. as global git opt, default-remote from git dir, normal-fetch-then-by-oid two-pass, 'at commit' annotation only when parent unpopulated). Also fixed a t7400 #96 regression: submodule add --force now reuses an existing .git/modules/<name> instead of remove+reclone (git only clones when sm_gitdir absent). Remaining 30-45/55/56 cascade from TWO OTHER subsystems: subtest 30's 'git checkout --recurse-submodules super' must fetch a missing submodule commit on-demand (checkout.rs, not fetch) - this blocks 30-45; and clone --recurse-submodules double-clones the submodule leaving src_clone uncleaned, blocking 55/56. Both are outside fetch-recursion scope."}